# Credentials for the live assistant (`ambient assist`), as 1Password
# references. This file holds no secrets and is committed deliberately; `op run`
# resolves each op:// reference at call time:
#
#   op run --env-file .env.assistant.op -- ambient assist
#
# Kept apart from .env.op so a release does not need the assistant's key and
# the assistant does not need the notarisation credentials.
#
# Create the item once with an OpenRouter key made for Ambient
# (openrouter.ai -> Keys); give it a credit limit:
#
#   op item create --category="API Credential" --title="Ambient OpenRouter" \
#     --vault=Private 'credential[password]=<the key>'
#
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=op://Private/Ambient OpenRouter/credential
#
# Only when assistant.base_url points at a Cloudflare AI Gateway that requires
# authentication: the gateway token, sent as cf-aig-authorization.
#
# CF_AIG_TOKEN=op://Private/Ambient AI Gateway/credential
